---
description: Defines standards for the API service layer, including Axios instance configuration, service file structure, TypeScript typing, and error handling aligned with the backend's ApiResponse format.
globs: "**/src/{api,services}/**/*.ts"
---
- All HTTP calls must use Axios through a centralized instance configured in src/services/http.ts (or src/api/http.ts).
- The Axios instance must set baseURL from the Vite environment variable `import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL`.
- Request interceptors must attach the Authorization token (e.g., Bearer JWT) to every outgoing request if authentication is enabled.
- Response interceptors must unwrap the backend's standard ApiResponse<T> structure and handle global errors (e.g., 401 redirect to login, 500 show error notification).
- Each backend resource should have its own service file (e.g., src/services/userService.ts, src/services/timeRecordService.ts).
- Service methods must be async functions with proper TypeScript return types.
- Backend ApiResponse<T> structure must be typed in src/types/api.ts:

```typescript
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  result: 'SUCCESS' | 'ERROR';
  message: string;
  data: T | null;
}
```

- Service methods should return the unwrapped `data` field on success, or throw/handle errors on failure.
- Never call Axios directly from components. Always go through the service layer.
